      "text": "VT-2\nDOERBIRDS\n\u201cEXACUE BELLATORES AERIOS\u201d\nCDR J. L. HATHAWAY NAS WHITING FIELD, FL CDR L. S. SCHAFF\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nFriday, 27-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 0625 MOONRISE: 2008 % ILLUM: 90%\nSUNSET: 1647 MOONSET: 0946 JULIAN DATE: 6331\nTOTAL ADV: 0 TOTAL FLY EVENTS: 0 TOTAL FLY HRS: 0.0 TOTAL SIM EVENTS: 0/9 TOTAL SIM HRS: 13.5\nQuestions:\nEP Question: SMOKE OR FUME ELIMINATION\nNATOPS: (T-6B) ENGINE OIL QUANTITY LIMITATIONS\nSOP: (T-6B) WHEN ARE HOME FIELD DISCONTINUED ENTRIES MANDATORY?\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nSDO ZAMAGNI, SPENSER 0800 0800\nSUPER SLACK, TY# 0800 0759\nWEEKEND CDO TOOTILL, JORDAN# 0800 2359\nVT-2 Key Contacts:\nSDO Duty Office: (850) 623-7222 / Cell: (850) 450-7508 USN CACO: LT Gainey\nFDO: (850) 623-7350 / 623-7428 / Cell: (850) 393-3199 CMEO: LT Goodpaster\nSAPR 24 Hour Help Line: (877) 995-5247 CMD Financial Specialist:\nVT-2 Ombudsman: (843) 503-8818 CFL: LT McKenzie\nUSMC CACO: Capt Bertella SAPR VA: LT McKenzie / LT Swann / LCDR Cannavo\nUSCG CACO: CDR Hathaway Suicide Assist: Maj Tootill / LT McKenzie"
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "[MON-FRI]-KNSE 0700-2300, KNBJ 0800-1745*, KNFD 0800-1745*(CLOSED FRIDAY), K12J 0800-1745*$, KGZH 0800-1745*, KNDZ 0800-0100; 0700-\n2300 (Friday)\n[Saturday]-KNSE CTO 0700-2300, KNBJ CLOSED, KNFD CLOSED, K12J CTO ONLY**$, KGZH CTO ONLY**$, KNDZ CTO 0700-2300\n[Sunday]-KNSE CTO 0700-1730 & 2100-2300, KNBJ CLOSED, KNFD CLOSED, K12J CTO ONLY**$, KGZH CTO ONLY**$, KNDZ 1700-2100; CTO 0700-\n1630 & 2100-2300\n*Closes at listed time or sunset, whichever occurs first\n$- RDO and CFR operating hours M-F. Reference R&I 24-07/11 for use w/o RDO or CFR present\n1. Annual Flight Physical and Dental need to be completed by the end of your birth month. Contact Class Advisor for questions.\n2. VR Sims are available to students in building 3125.\n3. Sim standby to check in with sim supervisor and wait in the sim building lounge until end of scheduled standby period.\n4. During weekdays, open OFT or UTD sim lines on the VT-2 flight schedule are available practice sims for VT-2 students. Open sims assigned to VT-\n2 will not be hard scheduled or reserved by any squadron. These are to be utilized on a first come, first serve basis for VT-2 students. Any TW-5\nInstructor Pilot requiring the use of an open sim takes priority.\n5. Marine Student PFT every Wednesday at 0630 USS Intrepid Rd Pull-up bars. Every Thursday Radford Gym NAS Pensacola with MATSG-21. Snivel\nas required.\n6. In-flight photography (PHOTOEX) is authorized on all IP/IP flights to facilitate the positive promotion of Primary Flight Training and the Naval\nAviation Enterprise, not to interfere or supplant scheduled training, and shall be conducted in a safe, professional, and risk adverse manner IAW\nthe requirements set forth in TRAWINGFIVEINST 3710.2 and CNATRAINST 3710.38. Squadron PAO review and CO approval is required prior to\nposting or distributing any in-flight photographs on social media or other mediums of communication.\n7. Students may be scheduled and shall be prepared for 2 flights per day from the FAM4200 block forward, unless specifically prohibited by the\nJPPT. For Cross Country Operations, you may expect to be scheduled for 3 flight/sims per day.\n8. Students SHALL ensure ALL CAIs are completed prior to the execution of simulator or flight events for which they are a prerequisite.\n9. All weekend aircraft MUST be signed for Friday or Saturday. No fuel available after 2000 Saturday at KNSE. No fuel available Sunday at KNSE.\nAircraft issue available Saturday from 0800-1500.\nMONTHLY CALENDAR \u2013 NOVEMBER LONG RANGE CALENDAR\nThanksgiving 96 (NO FLY) \u2013 26-29 NOV IP Holiday Party \u2013 05 DEC\nCDR Schilling LFF \u2013 15 DEC\nHoliday Leave Period \u2013 18 DEC-03 JAN\nXMAS 96 \u2013 24-27 DEC\nNew Year 96 \u2013 03 JAN\nLake Havasu Detachment \u2013 25 JAN \u2013 05 MAR.\nIP Swap 14 Feb.\nChange of Command \u2013 12MAR\nSAFETY DEPARTMENT OPERATIONS OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER COMMANDING OFFICER\nREPRESENTATIVE LCDR J. D. SCARFO CDR L. S. SCHAFF CDR J. L. HATHAWAY"
